                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "rectangle",
                          "id": "cUxDN",
                          "name": "divider",
                          "fill": "#E8E5E0",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "height": 1
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "SUjXb",
                          "name": "body",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 24,
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "zYqJx",
                              "name": "p1",
                              "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Sleep is the most underrated lever you have for energy, mood and focus. While you sleep, your body repairs tissue, consolidates memory, and rebalances the hormones that drive hunger and stress.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.6,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "tEaa0",
                              "name": "p2",
                              "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Aim for 7-9 hours of consistent sleep. Going to bed and waking up at the same time each day - even on weekends - trains your circadian rhythm and makes falling asleep effortless over time.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.6,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "ibdE2",
                              "name": "p3",
                              "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Limit screens an hour before bed. Blue light suppresses melatonin, and the dopamine rush from social feeds delays the wind-down your brain needs to enter deep sleep.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.6,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "lGZzq",
                              "name": "p4",
                              "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Your bedroom is for sleep. Keep it cool, dark and quiet. If your mind races at night, try a 4-7-8 breath: inhale 4 seconds, hold 7, exhale 8. Three rounds is usually enough.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.6,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
